stateDiagram-v2
    state "preloading" as Preloading
    state "ready" as Ready
    state "measuring" as Measuring
    state "closing-measurement" as Closing
    state "capturing-last-state" as Capturing
    state "draining-recorders" as Draining
    state "exporting-evidence" as Exporting
    state "retained" as Retained
    state "disposing" as Disposing
    state "verifying-cleanup" as Verifying
    state "completed" as Completed
    state "error" as Error
    [*] --> Preloading: admitted immutable profile
    Preloading --> Ready: required readiness and references
    Preloading --> Closing: settled startup failure, finish without hooks
    Preloading --> Retained: readiness deadline, producer still active
    Ready --> Measuring: beginMeasurement
    Ready --> Closing: finish before measurement records an error
    Measuring --> Closing: finish with callbacks
    Closing --> Capturing: close settled / absence recorded
    Closing --> Retained: close deadline, producer still active
    Capturing --> Draining: last-state settled / absence recorded
    Capturing --> Retained: capture deadline, producer still active
    Draining --> Exporting: drain settled / absence recorded
    Draining --> Retained: drain deadline, producer still active
    Retained --> Closing: readiness settled, explicit recovery
    Retained --> Capturing: close settled, explicit recovery
    Retained --> Draining: capture settled, explicit recovery
    Retained --> Exporting: drain or export settled, explicit recovery
    Retained --> Retained: retry while producer still active
    Exporting --> Retained: failed / unsettled / empty export
    Exporting --> Disposing: nonempty retained references returned
    Disposing --> Verifying: disposal attempted
    Verifying --> Completed: no accumulated errors, nonempty resource outcomes
    Verifying --> Error: errors or incomplete resource evidence
    Completed --> [*]
    Error --> [*]
    note right of Retained
        Resources and ID stay reserved.
        finish returns its cached result.
        retryExport replaces the cache,
        retains previous errors and can
        resume unattempted stages after
        producer settlement. Errors remain.
        Active producers and failed export
        block tracked cleanup even through
        parent disposal. Forced context
        disposal can consume teardown.
    end note
    note right of Error
        Error does not prove release.
        Release requires DISPOSED and
        attempted/released outcomes
        with nonempty evidence refs.
        Cleanup failure can retain the ID.
        No terminal cleanup retry or crash
        recovery, reservations are local.
    end note
